      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Given your soil pH of 6.2, blood meal is the better recommendation because it is less likely to spike alkalinity compared to bone meal. While both sources provide nitrogen, blood meal releases nutrients more quickly, which can address the visible deficiency faster than the slower-release bone meal. This approach will help boost your kale crop without creating the chemical imbalance that elevating pH often causes.",
