      "content": "thanks for the heads up on the foliage burn. i'll definitely keep an eye on the soil tests. one more thing—since i'm working with organic standards, i'm trying to get a better handle on the soil biology part of this. besides the N-P-K stuff, are there any specific microbes or underground activity i should be looking for to make sure the nutrients are actually being processed properly? like, how do i know if the soil \"life\" is actually active enough to handle the blood meal i'm adding?",
